---
description: Ground claims in files, commands, tests, and observed runtime results.
alwaysApply: true
---

For every load-bearing claim, identify the source that supports it. Separate observed facts from inference and unknowns. A planned command, model statement, or child-agent summary is not proof that work ran or passed.

Report what was actually checked, including failures and checks that could not run. Match the strength of the conclusion to the evidence: a unit test does not prove packaged desktop behavior, and an HTTP response does not prove the user-visible result.
